@startuml fs_content_04_seq_review
skinparam backgroundColor #0F0E17
skinparam defaultFontColor #E5E7EB
skinparam sequenceArrowColor #A5B4FC
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #6366F1
skinparam sequenceGroupBackgroundColor #1A1830
skinparam sequenceGroupBorderColor #6366F1
skinparam sequenceDividerBackgroundColor #1A1830
skinparam sequenceDividerFontColor #E5E7EB
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #1A1830
skinparam noteBorderColor #6366F1
skinparam noteFontColor #E5E7EB
skinparam titleFontColor #E5E7EB
skinparam ParticipantFontColor #E5E7EB
skinparam stateBackgroundColor #172554
skinparam stateBorderColor #6366F1
skinparam stateFontColor #E5E7EB
skinparam stateArrowColor #A5B4FC
title FS-CONTENT-04 (proposed) — AI draft, human review, publish
autonumber "[00]"

actor "Owner" as O #1E1B4B
participant "AI app\n(drafts only)" as AI #1E1B4B
participant "MCP" as M #172554
participant "Consent screen" as CP #172554
database "D1" as DB #052E16
participant "Review queue" as Q #172554

== Grant (once) ==
O -> CP : Allow, with the box Allow publishing and deleting UNCHECKED by default
CP -> DB : store the grant with scope articles:write
note over CP
  Checking the box grants the full scope. The list of connected apps
  shows each app as Drafts only or Can publish.
end note

== Draft ==
AI -> M : create_article, then request_review
M -> DB : article state in_review (revision actor is the connector name)
group The connector calls publish_article or delete_article
  M --> AI : refused, tell the owner to publish it
end

== Review ==
O -> Q : open the queue (in-review articles first)
Q -> DB : article, warnings, who made it, diff against the last published text
O -> Q : Approve
Q -> DB : BATCH: state published, revision actor admin
O -> Q : or Send back with a note
Q -> DB : state draft, note kept
AI -> M : get_article shows the note, so the assistant can revise
@enduml
